  "answer": "Fats are digested in the small intestine. The process begins when bile juice from the liver is released into the small intestine. Bile juice helps in emulsifying fats, breaking them into smaller globules. This increases the surface area for the action of lipase, an enzyme present in pancreatic juice. The lipase further breaks down the fats into fatty acids and glycerol, which are then absorbed by the villi in the small intestine.",
